/* ============================================================================
 * TapMyCar  Patch  Tow operator UX fixes
 *
 * Three bugs in screenshots:
 *  1) /towing.html showed "No tag scanned" because the contact.html
 *     v6OpenTowingPage() looked only at query params (?t=, ?token=), but
 *     the live URL is path-based (/tag/TOKEN), so no token was passed.
 *  2) The license plate was empty even though the tow operator scanned a
 *     registered tag (we already know the plate).
 *  3) The contact-page footer had no public link for general drivers to
 *     check if their car was towed (the /towed.html lookup).
 *
 * What this patch does:
 *  - contact.html: rewrites v6OpenTowingPage to read token from BOTH the
 *    /tag/TOKEN path and any of ?tag= / ?t= / ?token= query params.
 *  - contact.html: adds a small amber "About towing  check if your car
 *    was towed" link below the "Visit tapmycar.io" CTA in the active-state
 *    footer, going to /towed.html.
 *  - towing.html: on load, auto-fetches /api/get-tag?token=TOKEN and
 *    pre-fills the license plate input from the tag\'s registered plate.
 *    Shows a verify banner ("Yes, correct" / "No, edit") so the operator
 *    can confirm before sending. Falls back to manual entry if the tag has
 *    no plate or the lookup fails.
 *
 * Idempotent: skips files that already carry the new markers
 *   contact.html  TMC_TOW_FOOTER_LINK
 *   towing.html   TMC_TOW_AUTOFILL
 *
 * Run from project root:  node tapmycar-patch-tow-operator-ux.js
 * Safe to re-run.
 * ==========================================================================*/
'use strict';
